; Regression: MM2 variables are EXPRESSION-LOCAL.
;
; A variable-bearing expression must not shift the variable indices of any later
; expression. Before the per-expression scope fix in bridge_parse_expr_chunk, the
; file-global variable table made the rule below emit a VarRef with no matching
; NewVar, so the template instantiated an unbound variable and (b 1) came out as (b $).
;
; The two variable-bearing facts before the rule are the whole point of this fixture:
; every other mm2 fixture has at most one, which is exactly the condition under which
; the defect cannot appear.

(a 1)
(t $q)
(u $r $r)
(exec (1) (, (a $x)) (, (b $x)))
